  "data": {
    "body": "A block of mass $m$ is attached by a spring with stiffness $k_{s}$ to a wall at the top of a slippery ramp as shown in the figure. The spring's relaxed length is $L_{0}$. At time $\\mathrm{t}=0$ the spring's stretched length is L and the block's velocity is $\\vec{v}_{i}$.\n\nThe mass of the block is $m=5 \\mathrm{~kg}$, the angle of the incline plane $\\theta=30^{\\circ}$. The spring stiffness is $k_{s}=50 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}$. The relaxed length of the spring is $L_{0}=0.5\\mathrm{~m}$. The origin of the coordinate system shown is at the top of the incline plane, such that the initial position of the block is $\\vec{r}_{i}=\\langle -L,0,0 \\rangle = \\langle -0.60,0,0\\rangle \\mathrm{~m}$, and its initial velocity is $\\vec{v}_{i} = \\langle -1,0,0 \\rangle \\mathrm{~m}/\\mathrm{s}$. Use $g = 10 \\mathrm{~m}/\\mathrm{s}^2$.\n\nWhat is the net force acting on the block?",
